." Manpage for smi-agent-cli
.TH smi-agent-cli 1 "September 2026" "setmy.info" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
smi-agent-cli \- run an AI agent CLI non-interactively with a prompt file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-agent-cli
.I AGENT
.RI [ PROMPT_FILE ]
.RI [ AGENT_ARG ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B smi-agent-cli
command selects one AI agent CLI and runs it non-interactively.
The agent is not given the prompt file content itself: it is given a short prompt that points at
.IR PROMPT_FILE ,
and reads the file on its own.
The prompt file is written in s-expression (Lisp) syntax and defaults to
.IR TASKLIST.sexp
in the current directory.
.PP
Every agent runs in its print or exec mode with approvals switched off, so the run finishes
without an interactive shell.
Everything after
.I PROMPT_FILE
is passed to the agent CLI unchanged, for example the output of
.BR smi-agent-cli-options (1);
passing agent options requires naming the prompt file explicitly.
.SH AGENTS
.TP
.B claude
.B claude -p
.I PROMPT
.B \-\-dangerously\-skip\-permissions
.TP
.B cursor
.B cursor-agent -p \-\-force
.I PROMPT
.TP
.B gemini
.B gemini -p
.I PROMPT
.B \-\-yolo
.TP
.B codex
.B codex exec \-\-dangerously\-bypass\-approvals\-and\-sandbox
.I PROMPT
.TP
.B codewhale
.B codewhale exec \-\-auto \-\-output\-format stream-json
.I PROMPT
.TP
.B opencode
.B opencode run
.I PROMPT
.SH INSTALLATION
The agent CLIs install into the user's home, not as root, with
.BR smi-download-package (1)
and
.BR smi-install-package (1):
package names
.BR claude ,
.BR gemini ,
.BR codex
and
.BR codewhale .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
Missing agent name, unknown agent, or prompt file not found.
.PP
Otherwise the exit status of the agent CLI.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I TASKLIST.sexp
Default prompt file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.B smi-agent-cli claude
.br
.B smi-agent-cli gemini PLAN.sexp
.br
.B AGENT_CLI_OPTIONS=$(smi-agent-cli-options claude --model sonnet --reasoning high)
.br
.B smi-agent-cli claude TASKLIST.sexp ${AGENT_CLI_OPTIONS}
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-agent (1),
.BR smi-agent-cli-options (1),
.BR smi-install-package (1)
